{"owner":"saahilsanganeriya","name":"DINOCell","description":"","htmlUrl":"https://github.com/saahilsanganeriya/DINOCell","defaultBranch":"main","sha":"38e691d120fc731090f898c08b4ccbbff78f0a66","language":"Python","license":"MIT","fork":null,"docs":{"dinov3_modified/MODIFICATIONS.md":"8e4d3567d23d","dinov3_modified/dinov3/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md":"4c28f61de61a","dinov3_modified/dinov3/CONTRIBUTING.md":"b9f32594672f","dinov3_modified/dinov3/DATASETS.md":"945dd8ed6f4a","dinov3_modified/dinov3/LICENSE.md":"2b77e4839436","dinov3_modified/dinov3/MODEL_CARD.md":"e692f37a596b","dinov3_modified/dinov3/README.md":"647d8e7e60dd","docs/ARCHITECTURE.md":"fd45fecaceb5","docs/DATASETS.md":"ea538c3ca48b","docs/S3_STREAMING.md":"90257dc0268c","docs/SSL_PRETRAINING.md":"786d13625b0f","docs/TRAINING_GUIDE.md":"dd9f58dfca4d"},"pushedAt":"2026-10-12T03:25:55Z","fetchedAt":"2026-10-14T11:16:31.283Z","readme":{"path":"README.md","html":"<h1 data-anchor=\"dinocell\">DINOCell</h1>\n<p>DINOCell is an unfinished experiment in label-free cell segmentation: outlining every cell in a\nmicroscopy image without anyone clicking on the cells. It keeps the method from\n<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0319532\" rel=\"nofollow\">SAMCell</a> (PLOS ONE, 2025): predict a distance map\nthat is high at each cell's centre and falls to zero at its edge, then split touching cells with a\nwatershed. It swaps SAMCell's Segment Anything backbone for Meta's <a href=\"https://github.com/facebookresearch/dinov3\">DINOv3</a>,\nand sets up DINOv3's self-supervised training to continue on JUMP Cell Painting microscopy images.</p>\n<p>Saahil Sanganeriya built it alone in October 2025, after co-authoring SAMCell. DINOv3's code is\nMeta's and is included under its own licence (see <a href=\"#credits-and-licences\">Credits and licences</a>).</p>\n<h2 data-anchor=\"status\">Status</h2>\n<markdown-accessiblity-table><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Part</th>\n<th>State</th>\n<th>Evidence</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Self-supervised pretraining on JUMP (loaders, channel views, S3 reading, W&amp;B logging)</td>\n<td>Written; one run was started, and no finished run is recorded</td>\n<td>The last status note in the history records iteration ~220 of 90,000 on 2025-10-28: <code>git show 8e09a3f:ALL_SYSTEMS_GO.md</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Segmentation model in <code>dinocell/</code></td>\n<td>Does not run: the decoder fails its first forward pass</td>\n<td><code>UpConvBlock</code> in <code>dinocell/model.py</code> concatenates the skip connection, doubling the channels, but its first convolution expects the un-doubled count (<code>RuntimeError: ... expected input[1, 256, 28, 28] to have 128 channels, but got 256</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fine-tuning, evaluation, CLI</td>\n<td>Do not run, since they build the model above</td>\n<td>same</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Results</td>\n<td>None</td>\n<td>No checkpoint and no segmentation score is published, so this repository makes no accuracy claim</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>\n<h2 data-anchor=\"how-it-works\">How it works</h2>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code>microscope image (grayscale)\n   │  CLAHE contrast enhancement\n   ▼\n256×256 tiles, 32 px overlap\n   │\n   ▼\nDINOv3 ViT backbone ──► features from 4 intermediate layers\n   │\n   ▼\nU-Net style decoder ──► distance map per tile\n   │  tiles blended back together\n   ▼\nwatershed: seeds where the map is above 0.47, cell pixels where it is above 0.09\n   │\n   ▼\none integer label per cell\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The backbone can be Meta's released weights or weights continued on microscopy images. For that\nsecond step, each JUMP field of view is imaged in five fluorescent channels that show the same\ncells. Pretraining builds DINO's views from different channels (one view averages the channels,\nanother uses a single random channel), so the DINO loss pushes the backbone toward the same features\nwhichever channel it sees. <a href=\"docs/SSL_PRETRAINING.md\">docs/SSL_PRETRAINING.md</a> has the details.</p>\n<h2 data-anchor=\"repository-layout\">Repository layout</h2>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code>dinocell/              model (DINOv3 backbone + U-Net decoder), inference pipeline, CLI\ntraining/finetune/     fine-tuning script for the segmentation model\ntraining/ssl_pretraining/\n                       launch scripts and configs for pretraining on JUMP\nevaluation/            Cell Tracking Challenge metrics (SEG, DET, OP_CSB) and threshold search\ndataset_processing/    converts LIVECell, Cellpose and custom datasets to the training format\nexamples/              inference and SAMCell comparison scripts\ndinov3_modified/       Meta's DINOv3 with the JUMP additions (DINOv3 License)\ndocs/                  architecture, datasets, pretraining, S3 reading, fine-tuning\n</code></pre></div>\n<h2 data-anchor=\"setup\">Setup</h2>\n<p>Python 3.11.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\"><pre>git clone https://github.com/saahilsanganeriya/DINOCell.git\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">cd</span> DINOCell\nconda env create -f environment.yml <span class=\"pl-k\">&amp;&amp;</span> conda activate dinocell\n<span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> or, in any Python 3.11 environment:</span>\npip install -r requirements.txt <span class=\"pl-k\">&amp;&amp;</span> pip install -e <span class=\"pl-c1\">.</span></pre></div>\n<p>DINOv3 weights are not in this repository. Request access through the\n<a href=\"https://github.com/facebookresearch/dinov3\">DINOv3 repository</a>; Meta e-mails the download URLs.</p>\n<h2 data-anchor=\"pretraining-on-jump-cell-painting\">Pretraining on JUMP Cell Painting</h2>\n<p>Put <code>dinov3_vits16_pretrain_lvd1689m-08c60483.pth</code> in a <code>dinov3/checkpoints/</code> folder next to this\nclone (the path in <code>student.pretrained_weights</code> of the config), then:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\"><pre><span class=\"pl-c1\">cd</span> training/ssl_pretraining\n./launch_ssl_with_s3_wandb.sh              <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> reads images from the public cellpainting-gallery S3 bucket</span>\n./launch_ssl_with_s3_wandb.sh --no-wandb   <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> without Weights &amp; Biases</span></pre></div>\n<p>No AWS account is needed. The script tries to activate a conda environment named <code>dinov3</code>; if\nthere is none, it carries on in the active environment. The configuration and the other options are\nin <a href=\"docs/SSL_PRETRAINING.md\">docs/SSL_PRETRAINING.md</a>.</p>\n<h2 data-anchor=\"segmentation-fine-tuning-and-evaluation\">Segmentation, fine-tuning and evaluation</h2>\n<p>These are the intended entry points. They stop at the decoder error described under <a href=\"#status\">Status</a>.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-python notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\"><pre><span class=\"pl-k\">import</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">cv2</span>\n<span class=\"pl-k\">import</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">numpy</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">as</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">np</span>\n<span class=\"pl-k\">from</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">dinocell</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">import</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">create_dinocell_model</span>, <span class=\"pl-v\">DINOCellPipeline</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-s1\">image</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">cv2</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">imread</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\">\"cells.png\"</span>, <span class=\"pl-s1\">cv2</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">IMREAD_GRAYSCALE</span>)\n<span class=\"pl-s1\">model</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">create_dinocell_model</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\">\"small\"</span>, <span class=\"pl-s1\">freeze_backbone</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">True</span>, <span class=\"pl-s1\">pretrained</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">False</span>)\n<span class=\"pl-s1\">model</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">load_weights</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\">\"checkpoints/dinocell/best_model.pt\"</span>)  <span class=\"pl-c\"># a fine-tuned DINOCell checkpoint</span>\n<span class=\"pl-s1\">labels</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">DINOCellPipeline</span>(<span class=\"pl-s1\">model</span>, <span class=\"pl-s1\">device</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span><span class=\"pl-s\">\"cuda\"</span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">run</span>(<span class=\"pl-s1\">image</span>)\n<span class=\"pl-en\">print</span>(<span class=\"pl-en\">len</span>(<span class=\"pl-s1\">np</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">unique</span>(<span class=\"pl-s1\">labels</span>)) <span class=\"pl-c1\">-</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">1</span>, <span class=\"pl-s\">\"cells\"</span>)</pre></div>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\"><pre>dinocell segment cells.png --model checkpoints/dinocell/best_model.pt --output results/\n\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">cd</span> training/finetune\npython train.py --dataset ../../datasets/LIVECell-train --model-size small --freeze-backbone \\\n    --output ../../checkpoints/dinocell\n\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">cd</span> ../../evaluation\npython evaluate.py --model ../checkpoints/dinocell/best_model.pt --dataset ../datasets/PBL_HEK</pre></div>\n<p><a href=\"docs/DATASETS.md\">docs/DATASETS.md</a> covers getting and converting the datasets;\n<a href=\"docs/TRAINING_GUIDE.md\">docs/TRAINING_GUIDE.md</a> covers the training options.</p>\n<h2 data-anchor=\"credits-and-licences\">Credits and licences</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>This project's code</strong> (everything outside <code>dinov3_modified/</code>): MIT, see <a href=\"LICENSE\">LICENSE</a>.</li>\n<li><strong><code>dinov3_modified/</code></strong>: a copy of Meta's DINOv3 with additions for this project. The whole folder,\nincluding the additions, is under the DINOv3 License in\n<a href=\"dinov3_modified/dinov3/LICENSE.md\"><code>dinov3_modified/dinov3/LICENSE.md</code></a>, not MIT.\n<a href=\"dinov3_modified/MODIFICATIONS.md\"><code>dinov3_modified/MODIFICATIONS.md</code></a> lists what was added and changed.</li>\n<li><strong>SAMCell</strong>: the distance-map method and the default watershed thresholds come from SAMCell, and\n<code>dinocell/slidingWindow.py</code> is adapted from SAMCell's code (MIT). Its licence notice is in <a href=\"NOTICE\">NOTICE</a>.</li>\n<li><strong>Data</strong>: the JUMP Cell Painting images come from the public <code>cellpainting-gallery</code> bucket on AWS.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 data-anchor=\"citation\">Citation</h2>\n<p>SAMCell: Generalized label-free biological cell segmentation with segment anything. PLOS ONE 20(9): e0319532 (2025).\n<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0319532\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0319532</a></p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-text-bibtex notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\"><pre><span class=\"pl-k\">@misc</span>{<span class=\"pl-en\">simeoni2025dinov3</span>,\n  <span class=\"pl-s\">title</span>=<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">{</span>{DINOv3}<span class=\"pl-pds\">}</span></span>,\n  <span class=\"pl-s\">author</span>=<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">{</span>Siméoni, Oriane and Vo, Huy V. and others<span class=\"pl-pds\">}</span></span>,\n  <span class=\"pl-s\">year</span>=<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">{</span>2025<span class=\"pl-pds\">}</span></span>,\n  <span class=\"pl-s\">eprint</span>=<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">{</span>2508.10104<span class=\"pl-pds\">}</span></span>,\n  <span class=\"pl-s\">archivePrefix</span>=<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">{</span>arXiv<span class=\"pl-pds\">}</span></span>,\n}</pre></div>"},"tree":{"truncated":false,"withheld":0,"entries":[[".gitignore","b",565],["LICENSE","b",1078],["NOTICE","b",1770],["README.md","b",6654],["dataset_processing","t",0],["dataset_processing/__init__.py","b",44],["dataset_processing/dataset_utils.py","b",2309],["dataset_processing/process_dataset.py","b",10177],["dinocell","t",0],["dinocell/__init__.py","b",470],["dinocell/cli.py","b",4760],["dinocell/dataset.py","b",6983],["dinocell/model.py","b",13510],["dinocell/pipeline.py","b",15666],["dinocell/preprocessing.py","b",7418],["dinocell/slidingWindow.py","b",9490],["dinov3_modified","t",0],["dinov3_modified/MODIFICATIONS.md","b",2150],["dinov3_modified/dinov3","t",0],["dinov3_modified/dinov3/.docstr.yaml","b",91],["dinov3_modified/dinov3/.gitignore","b",195],["dinov3_modified/dinov3/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md","b",3537],["dinov3_modified/dinov3/CONTRIBUTING.md","b",1242],["dinov3_modified/dinov3/DATASETS.md","b",1952],["dinov3_modified/dinov3/LICENSE.md","b",7503],["dinov3_modified/dinov3/MODEL_CARD.md","b",12950],["dinov3_modified/dinov3/README.md","b",31541],["dinov3_modified/dinov3/conda.yaml","b",369],["dinov3_modified/dinov3/dinov3","t",0],["dinov3_modified/dinov3/dinov3/__init__.py","b",186],["dinov3_modified/dinov3/dinov3/checkpointer","t",0],["dinov3_modified/dinov3/dinov3/checkpointer/__init__.py","b",509],["dinov3_modified/dinov3/dinov3/checkpointer/checkpointer.py","b",13178],["dinov3_modified/dinov3/dinov3/configs","t",0],["dinov3_modified/dinov3/dinov3/configs/__init__.py","b",382],["dinov3_modified/dinov3/dinov3/configs/config.py","b",7682],["dinov3_modified/dinov3/dinov3/configs/ssl_default_config.yaml","b",6751],["dinov3_modified/dinov3/dinov3/configs/train","t",0],["dinov3_modified/dinov3/dinov3/configs/train/dinov3_vit7b16_gram_anchor.yaml","b",4354],["dinov3_modified/dinov3/dinov3/configs/train/dinov3_vit7b16_high_res_adapt.yaml","b",4535],["dinov3_modified/dinov3/dinov3/configs/train/dinov3_vit7b16_pretrain.yaml","b",3634],["dino